e analyst initially measured M1 as 12 seconds, but then corrected it to 21 seconds after checking the log and retracted the 12-second claim. The corrected measurement is 21 seconds, so the answer should be corrected with the value 21 and unit seconds. The original 12 seconds is retracted, so only the corrected one is kept.\n\nThird case is a conflict between alpha and beta about the dataset samples. Alpha says 10 samples, beta says 15. Both don't have the underlying file. Since there's no supporting evidence from the files, the counts are conflicting and there's no way to verify which is correct. So the verdict here is unresolved_conflict because there's no resolution provided.\n\nFourth case is similar to the second one. The researcher has h1 and h2. H1 says M2 was 43 milliseconds, but h2 corrects it to 37 milliseconds and retracts the 43. So the corrected measurement is 37 milliseconds. The answer here is corrected with 37 and milliseconds.\n\nI need to make sure each case's verdict is correct and that the explanations include the source IDs. Also, for corrected measurements, include the numerical value and unit as per the source. For the first case, since there's no resolution, it's not_proven. The other two have corrected values, and the third is unresolved due to conflicting claims without evidence.\n"},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":145500796209,"load_duration":2403917,"prompt_eval_count":477,"prompt_eval_cached_count":21,"prompt_eval_duration":2678323000,"eval_count":768,"eval_duration":142377103000}